    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b57ae45e_6f5c1c63",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanCaps.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-22T21:46:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So there are a few things going on here where I think we need the longer name to make it clear what it does. First background, when we bind a VkImage to memory we may bind it to a sub allocation of a large memory block or give it its own memory allocation (i.e. DedicatedImageMemory). Even if this cap is false, we\u0027ll still use dedicated memory if the image is \"large\". Thus useDedicatedImageMemory doesn\u0027t work as a name since we do use it regardless. It\u0027s a question of sometimes vs always. Next alwaysUseImageMemory doesn\u0027t really make sense since well using ImageMemory isn\u0027t really a thing. If we really wanted to make the name clear it would be, alwaysUseDedicatedMemoryForImages, but that\u0027s longer than what we currently have.",
      "parentUuid": "503cfad9_c0e3d061",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 44
      },
